WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.300
Luke 16

00:02.300 --> 00:05.580
He also said to the disciples,

00:06.120 --> 00:12.940
There was a rich man who had a manager, and charges were brought to him that this man was wasting his possessions.

00:13.660 --> 00:15.400
And he called him and said to him,

00:15.940 --> 00:22.580
What is this that I hear about you? Turn in the account of your management, for you can no longer be manager.

00:23.600 --> 00:25.280
And the manager said to himself,

00:25.280 --> 00:30.620
What shall I do, since my master is taking the management away from me?

00:31.200 --> 00:34.900
I am not strong enough to dig, and I am ashamed to beg.

00:35.820 --> 00:42.600
I have decided what to do, so that when I am removed from management, people may receive me into their houses.

00:43.860 --> 00:47.960
So summoning his master's debtors one by one, he said to the first,

00:48.340 --> 00:50.480
How much do you owe my master?

00:50.940 --> 00:53.200
He said, A hundred measures of oil.

00:53.420 --> 00:54.480
He said to him,

00:54.480 --> 00:57.940
Take your bill, and sit down quickly, and write fifty.

00:58.560 --> 00:59.740
Then he said to another,

01:00.140 --> 01:01.480
And how much do you owe?

01:02.000 --> 01:04.680
He said, A hundred measures of wheat.

01:05.160 --> 01:06.160
He said to him,

01:06.580 --> 01:08.100
Take your bill, and write eighty.

01:09.140 --> 01:12.600
The master commended the dishonest manager for his shrewdness,

01:13.060 --> 01:18.040
for the sons of this world are more shrewd in dealing with their own generation than the sons of light.

01:18.320 --> 01:23.080
And I tell you, make friends for yourselves by means of unrighteous wealth,

01:23.380 --> 01:24.460
so that when it fails,

01:24.800 --> 01:28.060
they may receive you into the eternal dwellings.

01:29.080 --> 01:33.260
One who is faithful in a very little is also faithful in much,

01:33.680 --> 01:37.780
and one who is dishonest in a very little is also dishonest in much.

01:38.460 --> 01:41.780
If then you have not been faithful in the unrighteous wealth,

01:42.180 --> 01:44.600
who will entrust to you the true riches?

01:45.460 --> 01:48.460
And if you have not been faithful in that which is another's,

01:48.860 --> 01:51.440
who will give you that which is your own?

01:52.600 --> 01:54.440
No servant can serve two.

01:54.780 --> 01:57.880
For either he will hate the one and love the other,

01:58.200 --> 02:01.080
or he will be devoted to the one and despise the other.

02:01.940 --> 02:04.320
You cannot serve God and money.

02:05.000 --> 02:07.000
The Pharisees, who were lovers of money,

02:07.300 --> 02:09.840
heard all these things, and they ridiculed him.

02:10.340 --> 02:11.360
And he said to them,

02:12.080 --> 02:15.360
You are those who justify yourselves before men,

02:15.740 --> 02:17.500
but God knows your hearts,

02:18.000 --> 02:21.820
for what is exalted among men is an abomination in the sight of God.

02:22.000 --> 02:24.320
The law and the prophets were until,

02:24.480 --> 02:28.540
John, since then, the good news of the kingdom of God is preached,

02:28.960 --> 02:31.220
and everyone forces his way into it.

02:31.780 --> 02:34.600
But it is easier for heaven and earth to pass away

02:34.600 --> 02:37.500
than for one dot of the law to become void.

02:38.480 --> 02:42.100
Everyone who divorces his wife and marries another commits adultery,

02:42.520 --> 02:46.320
and he who marries a woman divorced from her husband commits adultery.

02:47.440 --> 02:51.540
There was a rich man who was clothed in purple and fine linen,

02:51.540 --> 02:54.280
and who feasted sumptuously every day.

02:54.480 --> 02:58.140
And at his gate was laid a poor man named Lazarus,

02:58.580 --> 02:59.760
covered with sores,

03:00.060 --> 03:03.200
who desired to be fed with what fell from the rich man's table.

03:04.040 --> 03:07.920
Moreover, even the dogs came and licked his sores.

03:08.860 --> 03:10.080
The poor man died,

03:10.380 --> 03:13.360
and was carried by the angels to Abraham's side.

03:14.000 --> 03:16.620
The rich man also died, and was buried.

03:17.260 --> 03:19.620
And in Hades, being in torment,

03:19.800 --> 03:22.660
he lifted up his eyes and saw Abraham far off,

03:22.660 --> 03:24.460
and Lazarus at his side,

03:24.480 --> 03:26.720
and he called out,

03:27.340 --> 03:30.080
Father Abraham, have mercy on me,

03:30.320 --> 03:33.460
and send Lazarus to dip the end of his finger in water,

03:33.820 --> 03:35.140
and cool my tongue,

03:35.480 --> 03:37.980
for I am in anguish in this flame.

03:38.900 --> 03:40.520
But Abraham said,

03:41.020 --> 03:45.400
Child, remember that you in your lifetime received your good things,

03:45.780 --> 03:48.160
and Lazarus and like men are bad things.

03:48.800 --> 03:51.020
But now he is comforted here,

03:51.520 --> 03:52.780
and you are in anguish.

03:52.780 --> 03:54.460
And besides all this,

03:54.760 --> 03:58.040
between us and you a great chasm has been fixed,

03:58.460 --> 04:02.900
in order that those who would pass from here to you may not be able,

04:03.300 --> 04:05.880
and none may cross from there to us.

04:06.740 --> 04:07.880
And he said,

04:08.400 --> 04:12.020
Then I beg you, Father, to send him to my father's house,

04:12.540 --> 04:13.880
for I have five brothers,

04:14.220 --> 04:15.720
so that he may warn them,

04:16.060 --> 04:18.620
lest they also come into this place of torment.

04:19.620 --> 04:20.920
But Abraham said,

04:21.220 --> 04:24.060
They have Moses and the prophets,

04:24.480 --> 04:25.780
let them hear them.

04:26.620 --> 04:27.340
And he said,

04:27.760 --> 04:29.060
No, Father Abraham,

04:29.400 --> 04:31.580
but if someone goes to them from the dead,

04:32.040 --> 04:32.920
they will repent.

04:33.940 --> 04:35.100
He said to him,

04:35.500 --> 04:38.400
If they do not hear Moses and the prophets,

04:39.040 --> 04:42.460
neither will they be convinced if someone should rise from the dead.

04:42.460 --> 04:44.460
The End

